<title>DENMARK: Danish March reserves fall to 94.4 bln Dkk.</title>
<headline>Danish March reserves fall to 94.4 bln Dkk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's foreign exchange reserves fell to 94.4 billion crowns at end-March 1997 from 95.7 billion crowns at end-February, according to the central bank's monthly balance sheet released on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH RESERVES</p>
<p>				 March 1997    Feb 1997    March 1996</p>
<p>    Reserves (bln crowns)  94.4		95.7	 85.6</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement the Central Bank said its net foreign loan transactions amounted to 2.3 billion crowns in March. Four analysts polled by Reuters had on average forecast Denmark's foreign reserves would fall to 91.5 billion crowns in March.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
